  "h1": "Acorns Alternatives 2026: Investing Fees Compared",
  "metaDescription": "Acorns alternatives compared: Stash, Betterment, Wealthfront, Fidelity Go, and Schwab Intelligent Portfolios, with monthly subscriptions and advisory fees.",
  "published": "2026-11-19",
  "updated": "2026-11-19",
  "intro": "Stash, Betterment, Wealthfront, Fidelity Go, and Schwab Intelligent Portfolios are five Acorns alternatives for automated investing. The right choice depends on whether you prefer a flat monthly subscription, an assets under management (AUM) percentage fee, a zero-fee advisory tier, or a dedicated cash allocation.\n\nAt The Modern Wallet, we evaluate automated investing services by calculating the real annual cost across small and large account balances. [Acorns](https://www.acorns.com/) packages its automated micro-investing features into tiered subscriptions: Bronze costs $4 per month, Silver costs $8 per month, and Gold costs $12 per month. Acorns lists no hidden costs or transaction fees, charging just one monthly subscription payment. Its investment accounts are managed by Acorns Advisers, LLC, an investment adviser registered with the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC), with brokerage services provided by Acorns Securities, LLC, member of the Financial Industry Regulatory Authority (FINRA) and the Securities Investor Protection Corporation (SIPC).\n\nBecause Acorns uses flat dollar subscriptions rather than a percentage fee, small accounts pay a substantial proportion of their balance every year. A person with a $2,000 balance on Acorns Bronze pays $48 per year, which equals an effective annual drag of 2.4%. For a broader survey of robo-investing services, read our [best robo-advisors roundup](/roundup/best-robo-advisors/). If you want a standalone percentage-based fee structure, explore our [Wealthfront alternatives](/alternatives/wealthfront/) guide, view [Betterment-style comparisons in the comparison hub](/compare/), or check our [Empower alternatives](/alternatives/empower/) analysis.",
  "tableTitle": "Acorns Alternatives: Published Fees and Pricing Compared",
